				<div class="leftcol game_description_column"  data-panel="{&quot;flow-children&quot;:&quot;column&quot;}" >

					
												<div id="earlyAccessHeader" class="early_access_header">
		<div class="heading">
												<h2 class="inset">Early Access Game</h2>
					<p class="inset subtitle">Get instant access and start playing; get involved with this game as it develops.</p>
				
				<p><span>Note:</span> Games in Early Access are not complete and may or may not change further. If you are not excited to play this game in its current state, then you
									should wait to see if the game progresses further in development. <a href="https://store.steampowered.com/earlyaccessfaq/?snr=1_5_9_">Learn more</a></p>
					</div>
				<div id="earlyAccessBody" class="devnotes">
							<div class="devs_say">What the developers have to say:</div>
			
			<div id="devnotes_expander">
									<h3>Why Early Access?</h3>
					“Adopting an Early Access model allows us to receive player feedback and opinions as early as possible. This helps us to adjust the game design in a timely manner, fix bugs, and optimize the player experience. Additionally, this model also allows players to participate in the game's completion process, establishing a close connection between players and developers.”
					<h3>Approximately how long will this game be in Early Access?</h3>
					“The duration of the Early Access status depends on the progress of game development and player feedback. We plan to complete the Early Access phase in about 3 to 6 months, but this may be adjusted based on actual test results and development needs.”
					<h3>How is the full version planned to differ from the Early Access version?</h3>
					“We are planning to enhance the game with more elements, such as new chapters, characters, and missions, while continuously refining the game mechanics. We strive to deliver a smoother interface, more detailed graphics, and smarter AI behaviors. However, please note that game development is a dynamic process, and the specifics and timelines may be subject to change based on real-world circumstances.”
					<h3>What is the current state of the Early Access version?</h3>
					“The Early Access version is currently in an active development phase, where we are continuously adding new content and fixing known issues. Players can experience the core gameplay and some unique features of the game, but may encounter some unresolved technical issues.”
					<h3>Will the game be priced differently during and after Early Access?</h3>
					“During the Early Access period, the game's price will be relatively low to thank early supporters for their participation and feedback. Once the game moves to the official version, the price will be increased to reflect the increase in game content and the improvement in quality.”
					<h3>How are you planning on involving the Community in your development process?</h3>
					“We plan to involve the community in the development process in various ways, including but not limited to:<br />
Communicating with players on the Steam Community forums to collect feedback and suggestions.<br />
Regularly conducting surveys and polls to allow players to voice their opinions on the game's development direction.<br />
Showing the game's development progress and behind-the-scenes stories to players through live streaming and development blogs.<br />
Inviting players to participate in closed testing to directly experience new features and provide feedback.”
							</div> <!-- /devnotes_expander -->
